Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Named Indices and Metrics", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"23efa32a-a46c-46eb-b643-67ab36445a01"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0a807c1b-7755-4a04-a428-34e9c6d8eddc"],
 " labels indices by integer position and treats every leg the same. For \
physics on a manifold and for symbolic tensor algebra one needs more: every \
index should carry a name, a variance (upper or lower), and a dimension, and \
contractions must respect the geometry encoded by a metric. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`IndexArray`",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f3603e43-bad9-4c3c-a894-034df9784a92"],
 " subpackage adds exactly that layer in five stages: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Dimension",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Dimension"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"83a2596a-c333-4e66-8f8a-336302112738"],
 " describes a single index, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Shape",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Shape"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"6b627a2e-e331-4883-ac27-3e4c4ed270dc"],
 " collects an ordered tuple of them, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexArray",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f27edde4-02c4-4abc-a572-62fec4b366d8"],
 " wraps a numerical tensor with a Shape, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4340846e-4bd3-4ccc-9c00-40b6bdfe670f"],
 " attaches a metric for automatic raising and lowering, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MetricTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MetricTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"85fcc2b8-8491-4329-835d-aff65d48ff62"],
 " exposes a catalog of the standard pseudo-Riemannian geometries. This \
tutorial works each layer in turn so that by the end one is computing with \
Schwarzschild and Kerr metrics with the same comfort as adding two matrices."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"913a5d06-cc96-435d-9bd6-ff3141ad1653"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"PacletDirectoryLoad", 
  "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/TensorNetworks\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cb3fb455-4c7a-40f6-8445-62b2dff560af"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",Expr\
essionUUID->"9482028c-f0ce-4c0a-8c2a-474a72765832"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Why Named Indices?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0d01d0b4-ae1c-4c4a-acbd-2cce24ebc667"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In tensor calculus an index is more than a position. It is a label on a \
chart of basis vectors. The expression ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["T", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}], "\[Rho]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"02aa73b7-42dc-4467-9202-f4eb7321bedb"],
 " names three indices, declares two of them lower and one upper, and \
implicitly fixes which basis they live in. None of that survives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"43fa30ed-4699-415a-9491-6b84722084dc"],
 "'s integer-labelled hyperedges: the contraction graph is correct but the \
indices have no identity beyond their numerical position, and one cannot \
distinguish a covariant pair from a contravariant pair without external \
bookkeeping."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5918573-8c52-438a-8383-910ef6bad0fc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexArray",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"295794c9-7c7f-4149-8b5e-0315d39a5897"],
 " layer fills that gap. The data carrier is a stack: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Dimension",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Dimension"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8187739c-9a12-4028-ac24-4da31e0ee994"],
 "[d, name] holds a size and a label and uses the sign of d for the variance \
\[Dash] positive means contravariant (upper), negative means covariant \
(lower); ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Shape",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Shape"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"9c304ea4-c990-4e1b-a083-04186ce6d4e1"],
 " glues a list of Dimensions in order; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexArray",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"557dfae0-271d-4082-bd52-cb12f23e4d3b"],
 " marries a tensor to a Shape and validates the match; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"9b241f98-ef79-477e-835f-b4f982450956"],
 " attaches one or more metrics so that operations across mismatched variance \
can use the metric automatically; and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MetricTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MetricTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"43b82a28-fc6c-499b-8349-0ef8be2a4cf3"],
 " specialises that wrapping to a rank-two, square, symmetric (or \
antisymmetric) object \[Dash] precisely the geometric metric of differential \
geometry \[Dash] and adds a curated set of named built-ins."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7b73d3df-0b99-4111-aeb6-8e1c43f2fc90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two practical pay-offs are worth stating up front. First, every operation \
that contracts two indices can verify that the indices actually match by name \
and that their variances are compatible: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["v", "\[Mu]"], 
    SubscriptBox["w", "\[Mu]"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ef6246d4-5eff-48d4-8ee7-e8a496590f02"],
 " is allowed but ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["v", "\[Mu]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["w", "\[Mu]"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a2225337-96ff-4f89-b393-8863b76be069"],
 " requires a metric to fix the sign mismatch. Second, the same Shape data \
drives display: an IndexArray prints with its index symbols decorated as bars \
and underbars to mark variance, making the type of an expression visible at a \
glance. The remainder of the tutorial walks each layer with worked examples."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1e102512-03f1-457d-910e-ae1eb8796599"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Dimension and Shape", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3f8a44bc-4e34-49c3-9715-253b356d88b0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Load the named-index context. The IndexArray context is loaded implicitly by \
the main paclet but is also exposed for direct use:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5b63dd4-4ea7-4f20-a302-9ce108a03c02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`IndexArray`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"98767f7e-1766-4462-bfa4-3528d685050d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Shape",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Shape"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"4d891901-31ac-46df-bdc0-7680a5a5c6c0"],
 " constructed from plain positive integers gives upper indices with default \
names ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cfdf73c5-cea0-4cb4-acb4-937fe7e0e8e2"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["j", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed4ea65-2b37-4edf-b2dc-890deb535a3b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5c1a0a10-1f43-4c31-bdf3-235bc962a2ee"],
 ", \[Ellipsis] drawn from the latin alphabet starting at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f0c472ea-da23-471f-910d-d053317505bc"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b8cf5a8-47f7-4e8d-a407-f2a191359c9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
  RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ce00cbde-c02c-\
4672-a116-8fd65189f0f3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The two equivalent ways to introduce variance are to pass an explicit \
Dimension list with negative sizes for lower indices, or to use the (size, \
name) form where a negated name marks the index as lower. Both produce the \
same Shape:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e584ead2-3939-45f2-b913-9de4490653e3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "\"\<j\>\""}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<i\>\"", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "\"\<j\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"22ba78ee-6bfc-468c-bf7b-b024c3723ebc"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Property dispatch exposes the underlying data. The most useful keys are ",
 "\"Names\"",
 " for the symbolic labels, ",
 "\"Dimensions\"",
 " for the unsigned sizes (this is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayDimensions",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArrayDimensions"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"194b95bf-2d8d-46d6-a1df-3883e6332a66"],
 " on the underlying tensor returns), ",
 "\"Variance\"",
 " for the per-index Boolean (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["True", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d97c4c2e-9774-4c62-9cc1-73f5ccbe3a18"],
 " = upper), and ",
 "\"Rank\"",
 " for the number of free indices. Together they recover everything one might \
want to know about the index structure:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"37c92ca3-a240-4ecd-a80b-663c303bac9a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"s", "=", 
  RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3", ",", "4"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<i\>\"", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "\"\<j\>\""}], ",", "\"\<k\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 

 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"s", "[", "\"\<Names\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"s", "[", "\"\<Dimensions\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"s", "[", "\"\<Variance\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"s", "[", "\"\<Rank\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"1590d767-c7c4-4029-99bb-50aa13ea3c4f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Shape is the type and not the data: it is purely declarative and contains \
no tensor entries. Two Shapes compare equal under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Equal",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Equal"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fce3e536-42e4-46c4-bc9e-0b177d324afd"],
 " when their dimensions match (with zero dimensions treated specially), \
independent of names \[Dash] handy when threading shapes through \
transformations that rename indices."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e688cbc8-f2a8-4174-b465-2f83ef198d99"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.3. DimensionQ and ShapeQ", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f507b151-c2cb-4faf-a787-ae8b4abdcb7e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The predicates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["DimensionQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/DimensionQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"79ab5350-26a3-4d06-9766-f074695bbf03"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ShapeQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ShapeQ"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d5c2fd24-b2d0-42de-8217-370223142e2d"],
 " are the cheap validity check applied to each component before passing it \
to a constructor. A bare integer is not a Dimension, and a bare list of \
integers is not a Shape, even though the constructors will lift them when \
given the chance:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2a40bc91-5587-4ba7-a42f-c13e04f7ce92"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"DimensionQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"DimensionQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "\"\<i\>\"", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"DimensionQ", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2a6d20d4-\
7e0c-4035-a348-4125d88381a3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
ShapeQ mirrors the pattern at the next level: a fully specified Shape of \
Dimensions, and a Shape built from raw integers (auto-converted at \
construction) both pass; a bare list does not.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"140c19ee-8e70-4f48-b7f7-dabc89487458"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ShapeQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "\"\<j\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ShapeQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ShapeQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b659d4dd-\
fa66-4d2f-aa00-64408b62930a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. The IndexArray Object", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2a172276-7728-488f-900e-af00d288cf58"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexArray",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"9663a89b-706c-47e3-8041-afd33a4adc6a"],
 " wraps a numerical (or symbolic) tensor together with a Shape that names \
its axes. There are three ways to construct one. The most explicit takes a \
tensor and a fully specified Shape; ",
 "ArrayDimensions",
 " on the tensor must match ",
 "Shape[\"Dimensions\"]",
 ", and validity is cached at construction:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99d2e23f-a07e-4f5d-bdc2-b71a28d5bec2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"mat", "=", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"4", ",", "5", ",", "6"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"7", ",", "8", ",", "9"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ia", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mat", ",", 
    RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<i\>\"", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "\"\<j\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ia", "[", "\"\<Names\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"ia", "[", "\"\<Variance\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"ia", "[", "\"\<SignedDimensions\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",Ex\
pressionUUID->"bf89b02b-7a6d-4d04-84fb-15fc286cb40d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "A shorter variance-only form passes a list of Booleans, one per axis, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["True", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "96b237f5-2a08-4a01-9a5b-abcca050a620"],
 " for upper indices and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["False", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a6c4013d-9a05-4c08-9da1-dded5136f926"],
 " for lower. Names are auto-generated. The shortest form supplies only the \
tensor and lets the wrapper derive everything from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayDimensions",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArrayDimensions"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7ef4122a-465a-4b7f-8fd7-00c716eef539"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"939e5616-3d19-49f4-b6e4-854773bd46ea"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ia2", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mat", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ia3", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", "mat", "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ia2", "[", "\"\<SignedDimensions\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"ia3", "[", "\"\<Names\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"ia3", "[", "\"\<Dimensions\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",Express\
ionUUID->"13f866ac-329b-4857-9080-eb5cf690c9f5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two distinct subscript forms surface the most common manipulations. ",
 "Part",
 " syntax ",
 "ia[[i, j]]",
 " slices, calling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexPart",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexPart"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5c92e5f4-b498-4b66-959f-b8cf7eb7505f"],
 " under the hood; function-call syntax ",
 "ia[\"k\", \"l\"]",
 " renames or permutes axes, calling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexJuggling",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexJuggling"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"62013f57-80da-4ca5-8e1f-e4dbc51e4af6"],
 ". A negated name in the juggling form lowers (or raises) the index by \
toggling its sign:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"be9d416a-0f20-4e9f-9699-0064502deb92"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"m", "=", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1.0", ",", "2.0"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3.0", ",", "4.0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ia", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"m", ",", 
    RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<i\>\"", ",", "\"\<j\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ia", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<k\>\"", ",", "\"\<l\>\""}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Names\>\"", 
    "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ia", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "\"\<i\>\""}], ",", "\"\<j\>\""}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Variance\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ia", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Tensor\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7ec5d3b5-66b0-4a45-96da-b39bc802d02a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Familiar matrix algebra is overloaded to preserve the Shape: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Transpose",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Transpose"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "aad8fa62-9225-4bad-840e-a468414543e8"],
 " swaps both the data and the index list, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Inverse",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Inverse"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0c11d639-c92a-4094-93f3-61fb71e76c4a"],
 " inverts the data and toggles every index sign (because the inverse of a \
(1,1) tensor is naturally a (1,1) tensor with the role of rows and columns \
reversed), and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Plus",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Plus"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7a41d966-3fea-42cb-ba99-738138ecfa37"],
 " of two IndexArrays succeeds whenever the multisets of (name, dimension) \
agree, permuting one operand as needed:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29c8bccf-54b6-434b-b54c-6edefb88d19d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "ia", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Names\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "ia", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Tensor\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Inverse", "[", "ia", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Tensor\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f882a11f-3747-408d-bc64-8871cc74a0b6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Other useful properties are ",
 "\"Tensor\"",
 " (the unwrapped array; identical to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Normal",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Normal"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f39e3e81-99e0-4676-8626-b457c797e68b"],
 "[ia] for explicit data), ",
 "\"Shape\"",
 " (the full Shape object), ",
 "\"Symbol\"",
 " (the rendered glyph used in box form, with bars and underbars to mark \
variance), and ",
 "\"Symmetry\"",
 " (the permutation symmetry reported by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArraySymmetry",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArraySymmetry"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"cd0f4a14-7c22-4c99-a220-164d06d05c37"],
 ")."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"de679aad-f682-4d69-81f6-a9b8a0db4f48"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3.4. IndexArrayQ", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bb22f998-5cc9-494c-908d-4ddfcd2c1682"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The predicate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexArrayQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArrayQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"144976e6-9891-4639-a567-f7ba6ff927db"],
 " holds when the argument is an IndexArray expression whose wrapped tensor's \
dimensions agree with the declared Shape under any recorded assumptions. A \
bare matrix fails because it is not wrapped, even though every IndexArray \
constructor would happily accept it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f4fa6ee7-5fd7-4a6d-9662-df6d140cf59b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"m", "=", 
  RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ia", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"m", ",", 
    RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"IndexArrayQ", "[", "ia", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"IndexArrayQ", "[", "m", "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9d201800-\
ed94-4ced-b7dc-a846090ea412"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. IndexTensor and the Metric", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3c6393d2-5f78-431d-9d3b-56044b08be46"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An IndexArray knows what its indices are called and how they covary, but it \
does not yet know how to identify an upper index with its lower partner. That \
bridge is a metric: a rank-two symmetric (or antisymmetric) IndexArray on \
indices of equal sign and dimension. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"baa8e8e1-5aa1-454e-8b24-bba025e02ad3"],
 " wrapper attaches such a metric to an IndexArray (or declares the \
IndexArray itself to be a metric). With a metric in place, contractions of \
mismatched-variance indices succeed by inserting the metric automatically."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"17ed1c8a-8711-4003-afbc-513637ac7156"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "To see this concretely, take the Euclidean metric on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", "3"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8606e93d-e98a-4830-b215-26ab31f44d51"],
 " and form the contraction of two upper-index vectors. Without a metric ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["u", "i"], 
    SuperscriptBox["v", "i"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fdae8bb7-0cb5-4125-bd99-831308096d80"],
 " is geometrically ill-formed (two upper indices cannot contract), but with \
the metric attached one of them is lowered on the way to the contraction and \
the inner product comes out as expected:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73c58830-a50e-4ff8-9a37-77af43385be0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"g", "=", 
  RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Euclidean\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"u", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<IndexArray\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"v", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"4", ",", "5", ",", "6"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<IndexArray\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Activate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"IndexContract", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"u", ",", "v"}], "}"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Tensor\>\"", "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9a3f1591-08e6-427d-906d-47da15c91280"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The contraction returns an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Inactive",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Inactive"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "92bf3e2d-5eba-4dd7-8824-3d0688a67acb"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/TensorContract"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a5a37702-02f1-4d08-ac05-eb4ceb87130f"],
 "] expression so the index structure stays inspectable; one call to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Activate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Activate"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "32a2ec1b-886f-4dde-a62c-6fbfd89549d0"],
 " evaluates it. For the Euclidean metric the result is the familiar dot \
product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "\[Times]", "4"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "5"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "6"}], "=", "32"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"56f2446c-ff5f-46f1-99ce-572c3a3f73e1"],
 ". Switching the metric to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"diag", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "1", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4ceecdd8-96e3-4329-b7e9-39900d860454"],
 " (Minkowski) changes the sign of the time component and gives the spacetime \
norm:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13c7b90f-a1f3-46d8-9bc7-914c9f88ab4a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"g", "=", 
  RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Minkowski\>\"", "[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"u", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<IndexArray\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Activate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"IndexContract", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"u", ",", "u"}], "}"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Tensor\>\"", "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"260fae1d-820c-475d-8a3d-e6e86290b012"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lowering an index outside of a contraction is equally direct. Function-call \
syntax with a negated name swaps the variance flag, and behind the scenes the \
IndexTensor inserts the metric so that the data is mapped through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["g", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Nu]"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"faa38854-1e7f-43e6-ba5a-e2586598e0cd"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"50458867-0330-4d5b-855c-0409742fba3e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"u", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"Dimension", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<IndexArray\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Activate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"u", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", "\"\<i\>\""}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Tensor\>\"", "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6d0e4493-dd95-4c6a-b965-647d4b204e21"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The upper four-vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"668f44b1-f447-40d0-bb09-bd405131055d"],
 " becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", "1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4ec017a0-4ac9-406a-9757-bdd8d77fa998"],
 " under the Minkowski signature, exactly as expected from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Eta]", "00"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8c27d1ae-475c-4635-945b-cc84be602aa5"],
 ". The same machinery is used by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexContract"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"19bf2875-3390-4957-9b29-5875da983c8f"],
 " whenever a pair of indices sharing a name has mismatched signs: the index \
whose sign disagrees with the metric's natural form is dressed by the metric \
(or its inverse), and the contraction proceeds without further user \
intervention."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5397bfb0-3933-45fc-9c46-ae549cbad506"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4.3. IndexTensorQ", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"14013634-9868-41c9-9339-f9b6997a49fb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The predicate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexTensorQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexTensorQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b5d8ad7f-c999-4ee4-8a60-2ee2086e7a64"],
 " validates the inner IndexArray and confirms that each attached metric is \
rank-two with matching dimensions on the indices it covers. An IndexArray on \
its own does not satisfy the predicate \[Dash] the metric attachment is what \
makes the wrapping an IndexTensor:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"88108fa7-7af8-4eea-80e3-67e4d3c53125"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"m", "=", 
  RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ia", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"m", ",", 
    RowBox[{"Shape", "[", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"metric", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Euclidean\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<IndexTensor\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<IndexArray\>\"", "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"it", "=", 
  RowBox[{"IndexTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ia", ",", "metric"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"IndexTensorQ", "[", "it", "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"2147b44b-a17c-4e93-a833-f614518ce759"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. The MetricTensor Catalog", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4176f8a4-f355-4bd4-935a-494d0a0ec875"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Calling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MetricTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MetricTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"30cc4e19-91ac-4658-9084-bab23f8416ec"],
 " with no arguments returns the list of curated metrics. They divide into \
four families: the generic ",
 "\"Symmetric\"",
 " / ",
 "\"Asymmetric\"",
 " (and their field variants, where every entry is a function of coordinates) \
for purely symbolic work; the flat ",
 "\"Euclidean\"",
 " and ",
 "\"Minkowski\"",
 " for textbook special relativity; the Schwarzschild family (",
 "\"Schwarzschild\"",
 ", ",
 "\"IsotropicSchwarzschild\"",
 ", ",
 "\"EddingtonFinkelstein\"",
 " and its ingoing/outgoing variants, ",
 "\"GullstrandPainleve\"",
 " and its ingoing/outgoing variants, ",
 "\"KruskalSzekeres\"",
 ") for the spherically symmetric black hole in every standard chart; and the \
rotating/charged generalisations (",
 "\"Kerr\"",
 ", ",
 "\"ReissnerNordstrom\"",
 ", ",
 "\"KerrNewman\"",
 "). The cosmological cases ",
 "\"Godel\"",
 " and ",
 "\"FLRW\"",
 " round out the list."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1eecb083-8c31-41b2-99db-4a8496348da7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"442f1378-988f-4513-a942-b3096a46d4e5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The simplest non-trivial case is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Eta]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f0d65727-2561-4606-942b-987d08775fdb"],
 ", the flat Minkowski metric in mostly-plus signature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "+"}], "+", "+"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8a66df2a-ac92-45d2-bcf5-68afdde97db8"],
 ". The wrapping carries enough information to answer most invariant \
questions directly: signature counts, determinant, whether the geometry is \
Lorentzian:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c37677a9-9637-4e2d-a33a-3757c2637051"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"g", "=", 
  RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Minkowski\>\"", "[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<Signature\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<LorentzianQ\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",Expre\
ssionUUID->"209643a1-306e-49fd-a9fd-689787d37942"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 "\"Signature\"",
 " is reported as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6f9d47df-c6e8-409e-95d0-993664ed278f"],
 " \[Dash] three positive eigenvalues, one negative, zero null \[Dash] which \
classifies the geometry as Lorentzian. Built-in metrics auto-generate \
textbook coordinate names: Minkowski uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], ",", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "1"], ",", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], ",", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "3"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5bc80039-bb49-4069-bbae-0b4b3567e7c0"],
 ", Schwarzschild uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", "\[Theta]", ",", "\[Phi]"}], ")"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5f0fed5e-12b3-4627-8d6e-d901240da140"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7294f2ba-4459-4843-90f2-be488e1a06f9"],

Cell["\<\
Substitute Schwarzschild for Minkowski and the diagonal entries of the metric \
encode the line element\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cb6ea7d2-a347-49a8-affa-75ae56286c03"],

Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "2"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", 
          StyleBox["M", "TI"]}], "/", 
         StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]}], ")"}]}], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "2"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "2"], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "-", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", 
         StyleBox["M", "TI"]}], "/", 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "\[Theta]"}], "2"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"sin", "\[Theta]"}], "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "\[Phi]"}], "2"]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"a93a8b98-675c-4690-a505-54f1776c6498"]], \
"Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab600540-79d4-4c3a-af14-1871e15b112f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Reading those four coefficients off Diagonal[g[\"Matrix\"]] is the quickest \
sanity check that the right metric is loaded:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa83c098-ddc4-4f06-bb77-f9be4369fbc8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"gSchw", "=", 
  RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Schwarzschild\>\"", "[", "\[FormalCapitalM]", "]"}], 
   "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", 
  RowBox[{"gSchw", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUU\
ID->"6922c4ae-2bb2-42cc-9405-2d71b218df71"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Kerr metric adds rotation and breaks spherical symmetry into axial \
symmetry: an off-diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Phi]"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"22b704ca-86ca-40a9-92f3-10aec3afb053"],
 " term couples the time and azimuthal coordinates, encoding the \
frame-dragging of a rotating mass. With angular momentum parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9d024db9-1a3e-4831-9dc7-7f6bd41a986a"],
 ", the off-diagonal entry ",
 "g[\"Matrix\"][[1, 4]]",
 " is non-zero whenever ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"92049ed4-a31a-46da-a11c-1165d781e6b7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b4cae51-3110-4f72-93f3-21c4f6736056"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"gKerr", "=", 
  RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Kerr\>\"", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[FormalCapitalM]", ",", "\[FormalCapitalJ]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gKerr", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0e9f6f7d-\
15f0-4c2a-8bbf-13342c04c752"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Several derived geometric objects are exposed as properties of the wrapped \
IndexTensor. ",
 "g[\"Coordinates\"]",
 " returns the coordinate symbols, ",
 "g[\"CoordinateOneForms\"]",
 " returns the differential one-forms ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7fdfada4-70a6-4f56-87df-91d992d7b54f"],
 ", ",
 "g[\"SymmetricQ\"]",
 " and ",
 "g[\"DiagonalQ\"]",
 " query the matrix structure, and ",
 "g[\"InverseMetricTensor\"]",
 " returns the contravariant partner ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c25bd381-2487-4b62-a2fb-b0381d6412cf"],
 " as a new MetricTensor with toggled variance. The full property list comes \
from ",
 "MetricTensor[\"Properties\"]",
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d16099e3-850a-4b59-a199-239d4a75fb18"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The connection coefficients are also available, exposed through the inner \
IndexTensor via ",
 "g[\"IndexTensor\"][\"ChristoffelSymbol\"]",
 ". For a generic four-dimensional metric this is a rank-three computation \
and can be heavy; the result is an IndexTensor whose indices carry the \
appropriate variance for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}], "\[Rho]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8631d9fb-afe8-4448-acbd-483ae9bb7f88"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e3a5a262-86bd-4788-970c-e70a1bf49890"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With those five layers in place \[Dash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Dimension",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Dimension"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6061c884-e88a-44dd-9c76-15f4f867a16c"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Shape",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Shape"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"62cfd9db-d122-4297-ac88-1390b577eaa0"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexArray",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"834d6ea7-4280-4664-9099-46b9e7c1ce11"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"9a783e73-9c80-472d-973d-e8d461b4b0ba"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MetricTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MetricTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2a247072-617f-45c5-998f-80ae11616489"],
 " \[Dash] the named-index layer can be combined with the rest of the paclet \
for serious tensor algebra: free indices are tracked symbolically through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexContract"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"604ea023-eedf-46dd-bb0a-a727e5429e6f"],
 ", a metric does the geometric heavy lifting, and the catalog supplies the \
standard backgrounds for general relativity in two keystrokes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65c24a78-658f-42a9-8a9d-51d2459c507a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.5. MetricTensorQ", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b65724a3-6b48-4d18-9c7f-0e2efe77c9fa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The predicate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MetricTensorQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MetricTensorQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1ef7f107-2bc7-4d6b-89b3-3726bf4ff93b"],
 " holds exactly when the inner IndexTensor is a valid rank-two metric. Every \
named entry in the catalog is constructed to satisfy it, so it is a fast \
invariant check after any geometric manipulation:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cacbcdbc-3a89-4fe7-96ca-c753d379dd17"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"MetricTensorQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Minkowski\>\"", "[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MetricTensorQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"MetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Schwarzschild\>\"", "[", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",Expres\
sionUUID->"d947f77b-639f-4d14-a925-74c7a5b76128"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Array utilities", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d2737660-d66b-44a3-97b2-4c83adddeb0f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The IndexArray subpackage exposes a small set of low-level array utilities \
used by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexArray",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6485de14-e4be-4b03-aeef-3c384fa6f14d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexTensor",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexTensor"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2daaefc5-e8bf-4988-aecc-f0cca57bcb7c"],
 ", and the contraction routines. They operate on plain tensors and on \
inactive expressions (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "TensorProduct", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2821fccd-c8b0-49e7-a19b-f7e8ed3f1615"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "TensorContract", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"4ebb20db-6670-4c7e-bfb9-0a8d89eb8283"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "Transpose", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"eaaeb4a2-5177-42ae-8a84-4c46f722b303"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "D", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a4da1438-bd33-44e5-b5a2-00abf660f166"],
 "), tracking dimensions and simplifying nested expressions without forcing \
evaluation. They are useful when building or auditing IndexArray-based \
pipelines, especially with symbolic tensors."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"adb2569f-52b5-4150-9976-83397f5a9a8e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.1. ArrayRank", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"86545071-bd3e-454c-8c41-1008f7daf51d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayRank",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArrayRank"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"bf7f8e3d-8716-418b-8a09-ad2e01628542"],
 " counts indices, tracking through inactive wrappers. Contracting one pair \
of indices on the rank-four expression below drops the rank to two:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"80db9494-fddc-4302-af80-735b0f03b8cc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"m", "=", 
  RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayRank", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "TensorContract", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "TensorProduct", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"m", ",", "m"}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",Express\
ionUUID->"ef734056-8e9f-45ba-a46b-d53a05eac1e5"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.2. ArrayName", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0a428bc3-05bb-4758-b934-476881257805"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayName",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArrayName"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e079619d-bfda-40ca-ae39-e7bd2fbf9ab1"],
 " extracts the underlying name symbol from a VectorSymbol, MatrixSymbol, or \
ArraySymbol, and returns a bare atomic symbol unchanged. Anything that is \
neither symbolic nor a recognised symbol-array head returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["None", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "828b9b22-72b2-4e67-8b18-df365fdfad15"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9755a19-9a65-4430-9b69-e917fb6aaae5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ArrayName", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ArraySymbol", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[FormalCapitalT]", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayName", "[", 
  RowBox[{"MatrixSymbol", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[FormalCapitalM]", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayName", "[", "\[FormalT]", "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"4cd43ae2-8f7d-4581-9f10-0ecb61b092fa"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.3. ArrayPart", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"dd81a81c-0ef9-49a4-98c0-f996eb757d30"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayPart",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArrayPart"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e5a22ef3-47cd-411f-91ad-de8eced97117"],
 " slices a symbolic array while propagating dimensional metadata, so that \
the result is itself a typed symbolic array of the appropriate sub-rank:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9183600d-ae9a-4dae-9332-c30cbf2f6736"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArrayPart", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MatrixSymbol", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[FormalCapitalM]", ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3fe42f9b-3002-\
48cb-8f26-8f9119ae4f57"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.4. ArrayTranspose", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ac5c0a96-216e-4243-9ab3-47540ceb30eb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayTranspose",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArrayTranspose"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f3482955-75aa-4ab8-a6fc-8e97397350f0"],
 " permutes axes and simplifies, composing a nested ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Transpose",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Transpose"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1488d563-09b5-451a-b084-022f43212637"],
 " into a single permutation. Composing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "1"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"bc476dec-1b8d-4a35-877b-295300fb2be0"],
 " with itself returns the original matrix:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f505e3c7-b5ce-452b-b2e8-f29b2d6400fd"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"m", "=", 
  RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayTranspose", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"m", ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"9c597a6d-3f20-427e-86de-ae5d190ec7b7"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.5. ArrayContract", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0a6f338e-15a9-4114-b672-5e022bdfd4f6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArrayContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArrayContract"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b4572c11-9825-4442-bba8-7248fb692f63"],
 " contracts index pairs on a single tensor or on a list, which it first \
wraps in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "TensorProduct", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f884f54c-7e59-487e-84d1-d884a16eb416"],
 ", then simplifies. Contracting axis 2 of the first factor with axis 3 (= \
axis 1 of the second factor) recovers the matrix product:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"80e0eb25-5782-47bf-a41b-64101074c346"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"m", "=", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayContract", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"m", ",", "m"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"941aa73e-3678-416a-a296-72f0f5986ca7"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.6. SimplifyArray", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7ceb02e5-3dc3-459e-bab1-75955378c2ed"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["SimplifyArray",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/SimplifyArray"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"83be1cd2-4100-423a-af37-861cfeb30213"],
 " removes empty contractions, singleton tensor products, and identity \
transpositions from a nested array expression. A no-op transpose around a \
no-op contraction collapses back to the original tensor:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5689ce0e-5436-431b-9a11-568f8030f7d7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"m", "=", 
  RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{";", "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"SimplifyArray", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "Transpose", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Inactive", "[", "TensorContract", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"m", ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"Cycles", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"d8f9bef1-6421-4610-b8ae-cef560a7b23f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.7. ZeroArrayQ", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f74bb616-a217-4a84-8bcf-64e522a41813"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ZeroArrayQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ZeroArrayQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"74119e15-ff7b-4965-9fdd-aaa1bd5d5561"],
 " is true exactly when any dimension of the array is zero; it does not look \
at the values. The contraction routines use it as a fast bypass: any tensor \
with a zero-length axis contracts to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ad62d144-d9f6-42bb-aaeb-5ea545d43ec8"],
 " without evaluation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ffbebcf5-e0be-44f6-9d60-eb43048da80b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ZeroArrayQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "0", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ZeroArrayQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"d6d2f0f3-030f-44a0-af51-cd7b99681bca"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

